# Atlas — workers, effective-dated terms, audit log (Sprint 03)
# Login first (see auth.http) and paste the bearer token below.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Hire a worker (HR manager or org admin) → 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Maria Santos",
  "contactEmail": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "country": "DEU",
  "hiredOn": "2026-08-01",
  "jobTitle": "Engineer",
  "annualSalary": 60000,
  "weeklyHours": 40
}

### The worker, with the terms in force today (note probation fields)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers/PASTE_WORKER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Give a raise effective November 1st → 201 (an APPEND, not an update)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workers/PASTE_WORKER_ID/terms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveFrom": "2026-11-01",
  "jobTitle": "Senior Engineer",
  "annualSalary": 75000,
  "weeklyHours": 40
}

### Time travel: terms as of September (before the raise)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers/PASTE_WORKER_ID/terms?asOf=2026-09-15
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ...and as of December (after) — same history, different answer
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers/PASTE_WORKER_ID/terms?asOf=2026-12-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Retroactivity: terms before the hire date → 422
POST {{host}}/api/v1/workers/PASTE_WORKER_ID/terms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effectiveFrom": "2020-01-01",
  "jobTitle": "Time Traveler",
  "annualSalary": 1,
  "weeklyHours": 40
}

### List workers (org-scoped, cursor pagination as everywhere)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/workers?limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The audit log: who did what, when (HR manager and up)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/audit-log?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
